# =============================================================================
# OSP Tech — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Names only live here, never values
# (workflows.md A9). .env* is gitignored; if a real key ever lands in this
# file, rotate it (security.md 6).
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — the only two values that may reach the browser.
#
# The anon key is public by design: it carries no authority of its own and
# everything it can reach is bounded by RLS.
#
# Local development: run `npx supabase start`, then `npx supabase status` and
# copy the API URL and the anon key it prints.
# Hosted: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only secrets.
#
# NEVER prefix these NEXT_PUBLIC_, never import them into a Client Component,
# and never commit them. The service-role key bypasses RLS entirely. It is used
# server-side in exactly two places: the reminder cron job, and the shared
# rate-limit counter (`rate_limit_hit`, callable by the service role only).
# Without it, rate limits fall back to per-process memory — fine for local
# development, NOT for a deployed environment.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Site origin, used for canonical URLs, sitemap entries and OG image URLs.
# Local: http://localhost:3000 — production: the live .com domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 3 — reminder emails and the cron job.
#
# CRON_SECRET protects /api/cron/reminders, which runs with the service-role
# key and therefore bypasses RLS. Without this set the endpoint refuses to run
# at all, by design.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_FROM="OSP Tech <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
# CRON_SECRET=
